://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-17T10:53:23Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T10:53:23Z","body":"> * https://deploy-preview-1349--base-ui.netlify.app/experiments/toolbar/basic\r\n> * https://deploy-preview-1349--base-ui.netlify.app/experiments/toolbar/text-editor\r\n> * https://deploy-preview-1349--base-ui.netlify.app/experiments/toolbar/triggers\r\n\r\n@colmtuite What do you think about adapting one of these to be the hero demo or do you have something else in mind?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2662746410/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2662756477","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2662756477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2662756477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6etnB9","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-17T10:57:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T10:57:31Z","body":"> I found a strange behavior: the menu won't close when a submenu is open and you move the roving focus to the next toolbar element by pressing ➡️. Only the submenu is closed. See attached video.\r\n\r\nI think it's better to solve this in [Menubar](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/1407), perhaps something like a shared `CompositeMenuContext` to handle multiple menus grouped into a composite component\r\n\r\nCC @michaldudak ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2662756477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2662758623","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2662758623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2662758623,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6etnjf","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-17T10:58:24Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T10:58:24Z","body":"There are still a handful tests to add but otherwise this is ready for review @colmtuite @atomiks @michaldudak ~","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2662758623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2665305444","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2665305444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2665305444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6e3VVk","user":{"login":"colmtuite","id":805073,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNTA3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/805073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite","html_url":"https://github.com/colmtuite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T11:02:39Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T11:02:39Z","body":"I tested Toolbar in Chrome desktop a bit:\r\n\r\n- When an input receives focus, shouldn't its whole value become focused?\r\n- When focus is on a menuitem, and you press right/left, it doesn't move focus to the next/previous menu trigger. Is there a specific reason for this? Same goes for Select.\r\n- In the Triggers experiment, it seems like disabling controls doesn't work properly? When I disable the switch individually, that works. But when I disable the Dialog individually, that doesn't work. I saw this was called out before, at least in some capacity.\r\n- What do we think about treating numberfield differently to other inputs? Handling its behaviour differently, given that its value is usually just 1–2 chars long? Is there value in it, or better to leave it the same?\r\n- Why is there a \"Menubar\" experiment? Is this trying to be a menubar? Is it supposed to avoid the need for a Menubar component?\r\n\r\ncc @Albert Yu ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2665305444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2665487859","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2665487859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2665487859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6e4B3z","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T12:02:14Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T12:04:37Z","body":"> * When an input receives focus, shouldn't its whole value become focused?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ad46073-efed-471f-afbc-91cb7c170263\r\n\r\nFollowing the reference Michal shared, we decided that the focus should move directly to a text insertion cursor placed at the start/end of the textbox value depending on the direction you're arrowing in ~\r\n\r\n> When focus is on a menuitem, and you press right/left, it doesn't move focus to the next/previous menu trigger. Is there a specific reason for this?\r\n\r\nThis was a side effect of something else. We decided that this should be different from Menubar, for toolbar you should be able to arrow left/right from (possibly nested) menu items to an adjacent toolbar item. If that item is a trigger (menu or otherwise) it should not activate the trigger.\r\n\r\n> Why is there a \"Menubar\" experiment?\r\n\r\nIt's just an experiment to put 3 menus in toolbar which is mostly a generic roving focus group to see what gaps there are between this and a proper menubar, what can be shared etc\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2665487859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2666065159","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2666065159","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2666065159,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6e6O0H","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T15:32:20Z","updated_at":"2025-02-18T15:32:20Z","body":"> Following the reference Michal shared, we decided that the focus should move directly to a text insertion cursor placed at the start/end of the textbox value depending on the direction you're arrowing in\r\n\r\nHey @michaldudak just wondering if text navigation behavior feels correct to you now (in the [input demo](https://deploy-preview-1349--base-ui.netlify.app/experiments/toolbar/basic) and  [number field demo](https://deploy-preview-1349--base-ui.netlify.app/experiments/toolbar/text-editor))\r\n\r\n> When focus is on a menuitem, and you press right/left, it doesn't move focus to the next/previous menu trigger. Is there a specific reason for this? Same goes for Select\r\n\r\nAlso wondering what the behavior is like for this in your MS Office example, what happens when the select/combobox popup is open, one of the items is focused and then ArrowLeft/Right is pressed? \r\n\r\n(Ariakit does not let you arrow sideways out of a select in a toolbar: https://ariakit.org/examples/toolbar-select)\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2666065159/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2672070302","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2672070302","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2672070302,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6fRI6e","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T16:47:16Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T16:47:30Z","body":"> * In the Triggers experiment, it seems like disabling controls doesn't work properly? When I disable the switch individually, that works. But when I disable the Dialog individually, that doesn't work. I saw this was called out before, at least in some capacity\r\n\r\nOK it turns out various triggers have issues with the disabled state when they are not native `button` elements disabled with the `disabled` attribute (i.e. a custom element disabled using aria-disabled/data-disabled)\r\n\r\nThe fix depends on https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1445\r\n\r\nBefore some of these experiments seemed to work occasionally because I was passing the disabled state 2-3 times, to the trigger, the root, and the toolbar button at the same time, but it should only be passed once to the toolbar button\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2672070302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2673872992","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2673872992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2673872992,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6fYBBg","user":{"login":"michaldudak","id":4696105,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2OTYxMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4696105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak","html_url":"https://github.com/michaldudak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-21T08:16:45Z","updated_at":"2025-02-21T08:16:45Z","body":"I find restoring focus to the previously active item quite weird. I know ARIA guidelines suggest this (\"If the toolbar has previously contained focus, focus is **optionally** set on the control that last had focus. Otherwise, it is set on the first control that is not disabled.\"), but the applications I checked don't work like that. cc @colmtuite ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2673872992/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2678870879","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2678870879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2678870879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6frFNf","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T15:45:18Z","updated_at":"2025-02-25T11:08:52Z","body":"> * But when I disable the Dialog individually, that doesn't work. I saw this was called out before, at least in some capacity.\r\n\r\nI've opened a PR to fix this issue for Dialog/AlertDialog/Popover on their end: https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1473\r\n\r\nUpdate: it's merged","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2678870879/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2696674794","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2696674794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2696674794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6gu_3q","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T08:50:20Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T08:50:20Z","body":"\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9964a8c4-3f12-4bc1-8aac-e27b3b6b7f5b\r\n\r\n☝️ I've updated the toolbar input keyboard interaction behavior, see what you think @colmtuite \r\n\r\nAlso: what do you think about Michal's [comment](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2673872992) about restoring focus to the last focused item:\r\n\r\n> I find restoring focus to the previously active item quite weird. I know ARIA guidelines suggest this (\"If the toolbar has previously contained focus, focus is optionally set on the control that last had focus. Otherwise, it is set on the first control that is not disabled.\"), but the applications I checked don't work like that.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2696674794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2696922893","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2696922893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2696922893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6gv8cN","user":{"login":"michaldudak","id":4696105,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2OTYxMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4696105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak","html_url":"https://github.com/michaldudak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T10:06:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T10:06:05Z","body":"> I've updated the toolbar input keyboard interaction behavior\r\n\r\nIt feels OK to me. It's also consistent with the usual behavior of text fields when they receive focus, so IMO we can go with it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2696922893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2705784531","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/1349#issuecomment-2705784531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1349","id":2705784531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6hRv7T","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"h